WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.480
Every Christmas, churches sing
about a baby born in Bethlehem.

2
00:00:04.530 --> 00:00:08.130
But John's Gospel starts
long before any birth.

3
00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:12.170
In the beginning was the
Word, and the Word was God.

4
00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.730
Then it makes a startling claim.

5
00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:18.720
The Word became flesh,
and lived amongst us.

6
00:00:18.770 --> 00:00:24.790
So how can a baby born in Bethlehem
be, as Christians believe, God himself?

7
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:28.100
In this mission, you'll
unpack the word Incarnation,

8
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.010
which comes from Latin for in flesh.

9
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:35.300
Then you'll weigh up whether this is
the most important Christian belief.

10
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:40.090
Your mission: find out how Christians
believe a baby born in Bethlehem can be

11
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.400
God himself.
